#
# prima-materia — the twenty-eight lunar mansions of the Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm, I.4
#
# The tradition instance is pmt:IslamicLetterMagic and the work
# pmw:GhayatAlHakim; both stand in traditions/islamic-letter-magic.ttl, and
# this file is a repository unit only. It exists because the chapter is a list
# of recipes, twenty-eight entries each of which prescribes a time and names
# the works that may be made in it, and SPEC §15 counts every recipe as a
# capacity. One node per mansion: the unit the text itself gives, with its
# number, its name and its boundaries.
#
# Citation, as in the main file: the Arabic by book, chapter and mansion,
# because the page numbers of Ritter's edition are not recoverable from the
# text layer; Atallah's English by page; the Latin by book and chapter.
#

pmc:GhayaManzilaSharatayn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the first mansion, al-Sharaṭayn"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 1. Station steht, al-Sharaṭayn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first mansion, al-Sharaṭayn, from the beginning of Aries to 12°51′26″. The Indians travel and take purging medicine when the Moon is here. Talismans: for a traveller's safety on his journey; for discord and enmity between spouses and between two companions; for a slave's flight; for dissolving a partnership; because the mansion is fiery and malefic."@en ;
    skos:note "The rule the chapter attaches to this first mansion and repeats at its close: for good works the Moon is to be sound and free of the malefics and of burning, for evil works burned and afflicted. In Atallah's English the slave is made to escape or be released; the Arabic has only his flight."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 1, al-Sharaṭayn, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, pp. 19-20" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 1, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaButayn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the second mansion, al-Buṭayn"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 2. Station steht, al-Buṭayn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second mansion, al-Buṭayn, from 12°51′26″ to 25°42′52″ of Aries. Talismans for digging wells and channels and bringing out hidden things and buried treasure; for the growth of crops; for spoiling a marriage before it is consummated; exciting talismans, because the mansion is a fiery benefic; for a slave's flight; and for tightening the bonds of a prisoner when harm to him is intended."@en ;
    skos:note "The Latin has in place of the exciting talismans an image to make one man rage against another."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 2, al-Buṭayn, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 20" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 2, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaThurayya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the third mansion, al-Thurayyā"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 3. Station steht, al-Thurayyā"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third mansion, al-Thurayyā, from 25°42′52″ of Aries to 8°34′18″ of Taurus. Talismans for the safety of those who travel on water; for spoiling a partnership; for the bonds of prisoners; for the works of alchemy and of fire; for hunting on land; for love between spouses; and for ruining a man's sheep, cattle and slaves so that nothing stays in his hand. The mansion is called a mixed benefic."@en ;
    skos:note "The Arabic text layer is damaged in the middle of this entry, and the clause on prisoners is read from the translations: Atallah has releasing or torturing a prisoner, the Latin making the prison firmer. Both name the works of alchemy and of fire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 3, al-Thurayyā, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, pp. 20-21" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 3, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaDabaran a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the fourth mansion, al-Dabarān"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 4. Station steht, al-Dabarān"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth mansion, al-Dabarān, from 8°34′18″ to 21°25′44″ of Taurus. Talismans for ruining the state of a city; for a building that is not to last or stand well; for ruining crops; for keeping a slave with his owner; for discord and cutting off between spouses; for bringing misfortune on those who dig wells and seek buried things; for the perdition of whom one wishes; and for binding snakes and scorpions."@en ;
    skos:note "The Latin turns the clause on the slave round: the master is made to abhor the slave."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 4, al-Dabarān, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 21" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 4, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaHaqa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the fifth mansion, al-Haqʿa"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 5. Station steht, al-Haqʿa"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fifth mansion, al-Haqʿa, from 21°25′44″ of Taurus to 4°17′10″ of Gemini. Talismans for the welfare of boys and their learning in their religion, in writing and in the crafts; for the traveller's safety and the speed of a voyage by sea; for sound buildings; for spoiling a partnership, the mansion being mixed; and for agreement between spouses, provided the Moon and the ascendant are in a sign of human form, free of the malefics and of burning. The signs of human form are Gemini, Virgo, Libra, Sagittarius and Aquarius."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 5, al-Haqʿa, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 21" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 5, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaHana a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the sixth mansion, al-Hanʿa"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 6. Station steht, al-Hanʿa"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sixth mansion, al-Hanʿa, from 4°17′10″ to 17°8′36″ of Gemini. Talismans for ruining and besieging cities; for vengeance on kings; for bringing harm on enemies in every evil way; for destroying crops, trusts and deposits; for improving the state of partners and of hunting; and for disordering the action of medicines when they are taken."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 6, al-Hanʿa, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 21" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 6, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaDhira a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the seventh mansion, al-Dhirāʿ"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 7. Station steht, al-Dhirāʿ"@de ;
    skos:definition "The seventh mansion, al-Dhirāʿ, from 17°8′36″ of Gemini to its end. Talismans for the growth and blessing of trade and of crops; for the traveller on water; for reconciling friends; for keeping flies from entering a place; for obtaining what one hopes from a sultan or a great man one wishes to reach; for the welfare of a runaway slave; and for taking land, property or a house out of someone's hand."@en ;
    skos:note "The clause on the flies is damaged in the Arabic text layer; Atallah reads it as protecting the goods of a trade that would otherwise spoil and have to be made again."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 7, al-Dhirāʿ, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 22" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 7, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaNathra a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the eighth mansion, al-Nathra"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 8. Station steht, al-Nathra"@de ;
    skos:definition "The eighth mansion, al-Nathra, from the beginning of Cancer to 12°51′26″. Talismans for love and friendship between those who hate one another; for the traveller's welfare and the partners'; for prolonging the bonds of prisoners and captives; for ruining the state of slaves; and for driving away mice and bugs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 8, al-Nathra, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 22" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 8, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaTarf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the ninth mansion, al-Ṭarf"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 9. Station steht, al-Ṭarf"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ninth mansion, al-Ṭarf, from 12°51′26″ to 25°42′52″ of Cancer. Talismans for ruining fields; for exposing travellers on land and whomever else harm is sought for; for cutting partners off from one another; and for imprisoning an adversary and harming him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 9, al-Ṭarf, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 22" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 9, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaJabha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the tenth mansion, al-Jabha"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 10. Station steht, al-Jabha"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tenth mansion, al-Jabha, from 25°42′52″ of Cancer to 8°34′18″ of Leo. Talismans for reconciliation between spouses; for bringing harm on the enemy and the traveller; for tightening a prisoner's bonds; for firmness; and for agreement among partners and their benefit to one another."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 10, al-Jabha, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 22" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 10, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaZubra a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the eleventh mansion, al-Zubra"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 11. Station steht, al-Zubra"@de ;
    skos:definition "The eleventh mansion, al-Zubra, from 8°34′18″ to 21°25′44″ of Leo. Talismans for releasing prisoners and captives; for besieging cities; for the growth of trade; for the traveller's welfare; for firm buildings; and for the welfare of two partners."@en ;
    skos:note "Ritter's apparatus gives a second reading of this entry, with other boundaries, 24°47′ of Leo to 21°35′ of the same, and other works: turning the hearts of kings, nobles and brothers, and talismans for separation, enmity, illness, binding and destruction. Atallah's translation joins the two readings into one list, so that his entry for this mansion contains works that Ritter's text does not give here. The Latin follows the text and not the variant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 11, al-Zubra, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 23" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 11, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSarfa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twelfth mansion, al-Ṣarfa"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 12. Station steht, al-Ṣarfa"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twelfth mansion, al-Ṣarfa, from 21°25′44″ of Leo to 4°17′10″ of Virgo. Talismans for the growth of crops and plantings; for destroying a man's wealth so that harm comes to him by it; for wrecking ships; for the welfare of partners and the improvement of a craft; and for the welfare of slaves and keeping them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 12, al-Ṣarfa, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 23" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 12, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaAwwa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the thirteenth mansion, al-ʿAwwāʾ"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 13. Station steht, al-ʿAwwāʾ"@de ;
    skos:definition "The thirteenth mansion, al-ʿAwwāʾ, from 4°17′10″ to 17°8′36″ of Virgo. Talismans for the growth of trade and of farming; for the traveller's welfare; for consummating a marriage; for releasing the imprisoned; and for reaching kings and great men."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 13, al-ʿAwwāʾ, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 23" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 13, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSimak a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the fourteenth mansion, al-Simāk"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 14. Station steht, al-Simāk"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourteenth mansion, al-Simāk, from 17°8′36″ of Virgo to its end. Talismans for reconciling spouses; for completing a cure by medicine; for ruining fields and plantings and destroying deposits; for bringing harm on a traveller; for the welfare of kings; for the welfare of those who ride in ships; and for agreement among partners."@en ;
    skos:note "Where the Arabic has the welfare of kings, Atallah has the welfare of a slave; the Latin agrees with the Arabic and adds an image for destroying desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 14, al-Simāk, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, pp. 23-24" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 14, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaGhafr a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the fifteenth mansion, al-Ghafr"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 15. Station steht, al-Ghafr"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fifteenth mansion, al-Ghafr, from the beginning of Libra to 12°51′26″. Talismans for digging wells and treasures and obtaining them; for keeping a traveller from his journey; for separating spouses; for disordering the companionship of companions and scattering partners; and for driving enemies out of their homes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 15, al-Ghafr, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 24" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 15, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaZubana a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the sixteenth mansion, al-Zubānā"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 16. Station steht, al-Zubānā"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sixteenth mansion, al-Zubānā, from 12°51′26″ to 25°42′52″ of Libra. Talismans for ruining trade, plantings and fields; for cutting friends and spouses apart; for a punishment to fall on a wife if her husband wishes it; for harming an adversary on a journey; for discord among partners; and for releasing captives."@en ;
    skos:note "The last clauses are damaged in the Arabic text layer and are read from Atallah and the Latin, which agree on them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 16, al-Zubānā, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 24" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 16, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaIklil a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the seventeenth mansion, al-Iklīl"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 17. Station steht, al-Iklīl"@de ;
    skos:definition "The seventeenth mansion, al-Iklīl, from 25°42′52″ of Libra to 8°34′18″ of Scorpio. Talismans for the welfare and increase of livestock; for besieging cities; for firm buildings; and for the safety of a traveller on water. All agree, the text says, that one who makes a friend while the Moon is in this mansion will not see the friendship broken, and for that reason it is chosen for talismans of friendship."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 17, al-Iklīl, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 24" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 17, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaQalb a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the eighteenth mansion, al-Qalb"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 18. Station steht, al-Qalb"@de ;
    skos:definition "The eighteenth mansion, al-Qalb, from 8°34′18″ to 21°25′44″ of Scorpio. Talismans for binding banners for kings so that they prevail over their enemies; for firm buildings; for a slave's flight; for the growth of plantings and the safety of those who ride in ships; and for disagreement among partners. A prognostic stands among them: a man who marries a woman while the Moon is in this mansion with Mars will find her not a virgin, and the same holds in the mansion before."@en ;
    skos:note "Atallah reads the prognostic as a talisman for marrying a widow, a divorced or a deflowered woman, which the Arabic does not say: it is a statement of what the man will find, not a work he can make. The Latin has instead an image for conspiring against kings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 18, al-Qalb, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, pp. 24-25" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 18, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaShawla a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the nineteenth mansion, al-Shawla"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 19. Station steht, al-Shawla"@de ;
    skos:definition "The nineteenth mansion, al-Shawla, from 21°25′44″ of Scorpio to 4°17′10″ of Sagittarius. Talismans for besieging cities, prevailing over enemies and obtaining from them what is sought; for destroying the wealth a man holds; for cutting off and separation; for the traveller's welfare and the growth of crops; for a slave's flight from his master; for wrecking ships; for disagreement among partners; and for the escape of prisoners."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 19, al-Shawla, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 25" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 19, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaNaaim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twentieth mansion, al-Naʿāʾim"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 20. Station steht, al-Naʿāʾim"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twentieth mansion, al-Naʿāʾim, from 4°17′10″ to 17°8′36″ of Sagittarius. Talismans for improving a beast hard to break; for speed of travel and shortening the way; for bringing whom one wishes; for friendship; for straitening prisoners; and for spoiling the state of partners."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 20, al-Naʿāʾim, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 25" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 20, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaBalda a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-first mansion, al-Balda"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 21. Station steht, al-Balda"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-first mansion, al-Balda, from 17°8′36″ of Sagittarius to its end. Talismans for firm buildings and the growth of farming; for keeping wealth, livestock and beasts with their owners; for travellers; and a talisman by which a woman is divorced from her husband and does not marry again."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 21, al-Balda, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 25" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 21, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSadAlDhabih a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-second mansion, Saʿd al-Dhābiḥ"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 22. Station steht, Saʿd al-Dhābiḥ"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-second mansion, Saʿd al-Dhābiḥ, from the beginning of Capricorn to 12°51′26″. Talismans for treatment and recovery from illness; for separating those who love each other and spouses; for bringing about adultery with a woman one desires; for a slave's flight from his place; for separation among partners; and for freeing prisoners and captives."@en ;
    skos:note "Atallah renders the third work as causing a woman to be raped; the Arabic word is zinā, unlawful intercourse, and the Latin has nothing at this place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 22, Saʿd al-Dhābiḥ, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 26" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 22, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSadBula a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-third mansion, Saʿd Bulaʿ"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 23. Station steht, Saʿd Bulaʿ"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-third mansion, Saʿd Bulaʿ, from 12°51′26″ to 25°42′52″ of Capricorn. Talismans for treatment and recovery from illness; for destroying wealth; for separating spouses; and for freeing prisoners."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 23, Saʿd Bulaʿ, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 26" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 23, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSadAlSuud a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-fourth mansion, Saʿd al-Suʿūd"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 24. Station steht, Saʿd al-Suʿūd"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-fourth mansion, Saʿd al-Suʿūd, from 25°42′52″ of Capricorn to 8°34′18″ of Aquarius. Talismans for the welfare of trade and of the order between spouses; for the victory of armies and raiding parties; for spoiling the state of partners; and for freeing the bound. Whoever attempts the Art in this mansion, what he attempts is spoiled and is not completed."@en ;
    skos:note "The last sentence is a condition of failure and the only one among the twenty-eight entries: a stated outcome of working at the wrong time, which a practitioner could hold against the record of what he began when. The Arabic word is al-ṣināʿa, the Art, and the Latin agrees, giving an image for obstructing the magisterium so that it is not completed. Atallah translates it as starting a trade, which turns a statement about the alchemical work into one about commerce."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 24, Saʿd al-Suʿūd, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 26" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 24, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaSadAlAkhbiya a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-fifth mansion, Saʿd al-Akhbiya"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 25. Station steht, Saʿd al-Akhbiya"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-fifth mansion, Saʿd al-Akhbiya, from 8°34′18″ to 21°25′44″ of Aquarius. Talismans for besieging cities; for harming enemies, prevailing over them and bringing evil on them; for sending messengers and spies and their success; for cutting spouses apart and ruining crops; for binding a husband and every limb; for binding the prisoner; and for laying the foundations of buildings firm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 25, Saʿd al-Akhbiya, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 26" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 25, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaFarghAlMuqaddam a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-sixth mansion, al-Fargh al-Muqaddam"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 26. Station steht, al-Fargh al-Muqaddam"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-sixth mansion, al-Fargh al-Muqaddam, from 21°25′44″ of Aquarius to 4°17′10″ of Pisces. Talismans for every kind of good; for joining souls in affection; for attaining his wish for one who intends a journey; for firm buildings; for the safety of travellers in ships; for spoiling the state of partners; and for the bonds of the prisoner and their weight."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 26, al-Fargh al-Muqaddam, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 27" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 26, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaFarghAlMuakhkhar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-seventh mansion, al-Fargh al-Muʾakhkhar"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 27. Station steht, al-Fargh al-Muʾakhkhar"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-seventh mansion, al-Fargh al-Muʾakhkhar, from 4°17′10″ to 17°8′36″ of Pisces. Talismans for the growth of trade and the blessing of crops; for quick recovery from illness; for destroying the wealth of whom one wishes; for spoiling the state between spouses; for harming those who ride in ships; for prolonging a prisoner's detention; and for harming slaves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Ghāyat al-Ḥakīm I.4, mansion 27, al-Fargh al-Muʾakhkhar, ed. H. Ritter (1933)" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix (Ghayat al-Hakim), The Goal of the Wise, trans. Hashem Atallah, vol. I, p. 27" ;
    dcterms:source "Picatrix Latinus I.4, mansion 27, ed. D. Pingree (London: Warburg Institute, 1986)" .

pmc:GhayaManzilaRisha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:GhayatAlHakim ;
    rdfs:label "Talismans made while the Moon is in the twenty-eighth mansion, al-Rishāʾ"@en, "Talismane, gefertigt, während der Mond in der 28. Station steht, al-Rishāʾ"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-eighth mansion, al-Rishāʾ, from 17°8′36″ of Pisces to its end. Talismans for trade and the growth of farming; for treatment of illness; for destroying deposits; for the traveller's safety; for reconciling spouses; for the bonds of prisoners and their weight; and for harming those who ride in ships."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:IslamicLetterMagic ;
